#. Diagram label
msgid "Publish a web app — declared, translated, built at its own route"
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/web-app-publish.bpmn:87
#. Diagram label
msgid "Review the size against its budget"
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/web-app-publish.bpmn:77
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The author fixes what the check named (the manifest, the lockfile, a clashing id, a stale template) and commits again. A translation that dropped a placeholder goes back to its locale's translator through the same PR route."
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/web-app-publish.bpmn:61
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The harness's multi-locale translation, unchanged: the templates are merged into each locale's `.po`, new and fuzzy strings are translated with the fixed terms, the gates run, and each locale is its own PR. Afterwards the translation watcher (`Process_TranslationRefresh`) keeps them current as the catalog moves."
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/web-app-publish.bpmn:89
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The index flags an app over its `sizeBudgetMB`; the site size review reads it with the rest of the site. Over budget is a finding for the author, never a silent publish."
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/web-app-publish.bpmn:49
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The layer declares a directory of kind `web-app` in its `<name>.json` and puts a `web-app.json` (`web-app/0.1.0`) at its root: id, title, description, how it builds, the languages it ships (the site's six UN languages: ar, en, es, fr, ru, zh), the layer directories it reads at build time (`contentFrom`), a size budget, and for a copied app its licence and source. Its UI strings are one flat catalog in the source language (`i18n.catalog`). No publish script, no `site.build.keep`, no harness of its own."
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/web-app-publish.bpmn:24
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The person or agent who holds the app's source in a content layer. They declare it; they never write a publish script for it."
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/web-app-publish.bpmn:39
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The source-language lead and the locale translators of the harness's translation process. The app's strings are one more template to them."
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/web-app-publish.bpmn:66
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Tool `web-app-build` (`web-apps:build --check`): the manifest parses, `package.json` has the build script, a lockfile pins exact versions, no two layers claim one app id, every template is current, and no translation drops or adds a `{placeholder}`. Untranslated strings are reported, not failed: the app falls back to the source text per string."
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/web-app-publish.bpmn:55
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Tool `web-app-build` (`web-apps:build --extract`): the catalog becomes `translations/<locale>/apps/<id>.pot` in the declaring layer, one `ui-string` entry per key with the key as `msgctxt`. This is the app's \"refresh the templates\" step, named in the layer's AGENTS.md so the translation watcher runs it too."
msgstr ""

#: processes/ui/web-app-publish.bpmn:83
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Tool `web-app-build` (`web-apps:build`, run with the other declared visualiser writers): each locale's strings are written to `<i18n.out>/<locale>.json` from the `.po` (building is the injection), the app installs from its lockfile and builds, and the build is copied to `<locale>/<harness>/apps/<id>/` with every page marked `folio-navbar: none` and `rendered-by: web-app-build`; the `apps/` index lists every app with its size. No other page embeds an app, so it loads only when a reader opens its route."
msgstr ""

